---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import Led from "./Led.astro";
import settings from "../assets/screenshots/settings.png";
import prepare from "../assets/screenshots/prepare.png";
const strips = [
  ["01", "DRUMS", "delay"],
  ["02", "BASS", "reverb"],
  ["03", "INSTR", "bus3"],
  ["04", "VOCALS", "cream"],
] as const;
---
<Section id="split" index="06" title="Split a song" kicker="no stems? drop the full tune">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-cream/90">
        Drop a full song (WAV, MP3, AIFF, FLAC, M4A…) in <strong>SPLIT A SONG</strong>. Drums, bass, instruments and vocals land
        on strips 1 to 4, the original goes to the pool for A/B listening. A tune already split reopens without recomputing.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-4">
        {strips.map(([n, name, color]) => (
          <li class="rounded border-[1.5px] border-border bg-surface p-4">
            <p class="mono text-[11px] text-dim">strip {n}</p>
            <p class="label-wide mt-2 text-lg">{name}</p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <Led color={color} />
              <span class="h-1 grow bg-border"><span class="block h-full bg-cream" style="width:78%"></span></span>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-cream/90">
        <strong>A whole set at once.</strong> Drop several songs, or a folder, in <strong>PREPARE SONGS</strong> (or File ▸ Prepare
        Songs…). They are split one after the other, and each one becomes a ready <span class="mono text-[0.85em] text-cream">.dubstem</span> project next to
        its stems. Add songs while it runs, remove or reorder the waiting ones, or cancel all: finished songs stay. The time left
        shows at the top, and a notification tells you when the set is ready.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">
        The separation runs on the CPU with <span class="text-cream">htdemucs_ft</span> through ONNX Runtime: roughly 1.2× the song's
        length on an M3 Pro, up to 9 GB of memory. The four model files (663 MB) are not in the app: they are downloaded from
        Hugging Face on first use, after asking you, and can be deleted from Settings at any time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="lg:justify-self-end">
      <Image src={settings} alt="DubStemMix settings: output device, buffer size, recordings folder, pre/post-fader per bus, stem separation engine" width={360} format="webp" loading="lazy" class="border border-border" />
      <figcaption class="mono mt-3 text-[11px] text-dim">Settings (⌘,): device, buffer, folders, pre/post per bus, separation engine.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <figure class="mt-12">
    <Image src={prepare} alt="DubStemMix, Prepare Songs: a queue of six songs, one ready, one failed, one splitting, three waiting" width={1440} format="webp" loading="lazy" class="w-full border border-border" />
    <figcaption class="mono mt-3 text-[11px] text-dim">Prepare Songs: one song after the other, a ready project for each.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</Section>
